<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Menelik II</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Menelik II was Emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> from 1889 to 1913. He expanded and centralised the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire</a> and founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/addis-ababa">Addis Ababa</a> as its capital. His victory over the Italians at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-adwa">Adwa</a> in 1896 forced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> to recognise Ethiopian independence and became a grievance driving later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-empire">Italian Empire</a> expansionism.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/menelik-ii.jpg" alt="Menelik II" width="320" height="399" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Menelik_II_in_coronation_garb,_Emperor_of_Ethiopia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
